{"id": "clm:fefc6a41a4757ad297ddcd4d1e0d73e33fb1bb68549e3ab175fb7f0b40098102", "type": "statement", "text": "The _id timestamp shortcut needs extended-range date handling. SERVER-94207 reproduces a pre-1970 equality query yielding an incorrect EOF plan and identifies conflicting generated bucket predicates as the suspected mechanism. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-94207", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5cdbac8b809e3bf822663f381829be173d063a6f0c9a338090fff213e208d667", "ev:d4071e04abb03acdba05e734925ebb10e888e182baf573892714e699ce79c664"]}
{"id": "clm:71a9d428b5f1f96bbb84d2b5b373da67c2ebf0ff716c7491799a2aa0e9bdd6e7", "type": "statement", "text": "SERVER-99527 documents a historical correctness failure: a non-metaField delete can advance control.min while leaving the bucket _id timestamp unchanged; later indexed reopening can admit measurements outside the _id-derived span and time filters can omit results. Its August 7, 2025 advisory identifies affected 7.0.0–7.0.15 and 8.0.0–8.0.3 releases; both related tickets list fixes including 7.0.16 and 8.0.4. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2025-08-07)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-99527", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-94559"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2f785a2cd2ed3e73712030c6b363db9176390e511b4fc01f4c993f603aa53b49", "ev:5cd9f073a43d5de78918f15d856e1f6be530f936d2769106dfa7d726e8c106da", "ev:cc708a42d6d2fc1f9fd426db2ff3357df0a4146cbfc7432150479960c7ce8bdd"]}
{"id": "clm:13edc84ca9b34d70a23c6b89d0c935a895f4742a8f5df687e6165105fe27544f", "type": "statement", "text": "Bucket _id comparisons are an additional rewrite that can enable bounded clustered scans. They require knowledge that the shard has no extended-range time values; BucketSpec warns that mongos cannot assume another shard has the same extended-range state. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_spec.h", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d4cf6765beeaabfe463b0324576fe8acbb2dea69a773970e115bba5cb41e658", "ev:58f2e5dc92d33902392f8daaf8cefd8be222f57e5ca07aadfdf0f87b207dd3f1", "ev:f8a2a6e00483ce4478ad591540415e6ac57640442f49bde51a264d2b0dbe5b6a"]}
{"id": "clm:75d56fb0685399599f58084215d51b6c29b725f32e2229ebfff5a42f4b171eb3", "type": "statement", "text": "Increasing granularity changes the span used for future time-predicate expansion but does not rewrite existing buckets. A validation check that rounds an old bucket using the new granularity can falsely report a min/max violation; SERVER-95480 documents this case. A validation warning alone does not establish that a time query lost data. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-95480"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2df9c44e0da81a2dc5b328460e1eede55e778dfcb7956908e85726c428104d11", "ev:5cda557fa3f5d3e9265924f7f42b8c232d4e95289a1c20f433c5fef92485713e"]}
{"id": "clm:48a2440e0d37108a314c79271c46ccee965e51053b4d5cff99681ed5c4bced47", "type": "statement", "text": "control.min for the time field is rounded down when the bucket opens. It need not equal the earliest stored measurement timestamp. The bucket ObjectId time differs from a measurement ObjectId time, which typically reflects insertion. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/timeseries/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:51c2a68a44571d63a101f7f64e4f4eb2fd597a5dd13c8bd066b7a9f705b27369", "ev:a949d34a779a03e9e2a0d0985113dca7bff85d23cfc376cbb619bcc277769758"]}
{"id": "clm:9c92a4788a894ead35f7a1bee9e6e40bfedc83630c8e8b9414a37841aaab2b64", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB rewrites timeField comparisons into bucket control.min/control.max predicates before unpacking; eligible time predicates also generate bucket _id bounds that can enable bounded clustered scans. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/mongodb-5-0-time-series-collections/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:58f2e5dc92d33902392f8daaf8cefd8be222f57e5ca07aadfdf0f87b207dd3f1", "ev:6c997b49504d49ebcac59196fd240a675489ea74525e2c37149f37ed69f0b6c9"]}
{"id": "clm:602e8823b6e0cd62c00f0e1fe33361f32798c65ea4e2657b87d778ecd3b29c98", "type": "statement", "text": "For a BSON Date equality t = T, the default generator requires min <= T and max >= T, and adds min >= T - S and max <= T + S, where S is bucketMaxSpanSeconds. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d4071e04abb03acdba05e734925ebb10e888e182baf573892714e699ce79c664"]}
{"id": "clm:cc416f075bbd28c3df5f8c55dbfe9d661547e305d78cf8c4ce5199e470cac367", "type": "statement", "text": "For default time buckets, t > T or t >= T compares control.max to T and control.min to T - S, preserving strictness. Conversely, t < T or t <= T compares control.min to T and control.max to T + S. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d4071e04abb03acdba05e734925ebb10e888e182baf573892714e699ce79c664"]}
{"id": "clm:4f789b7270b82f37d10aed6f04381d6f46e95354b6e0d69d4c6c5064ef66caae", "type": "statement", "text": "Fixed-bucket time rewriting rounds the lower bound to the bucket boundary. Boundary-aligned $gte and $lt predicates can remove the event filter; $gt, $lte and equality still require measurement filtering. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:78a7cbaa18370723d23a4b72b60978c2d3744d9419614be759a0b4fed008aae1", "ev:bc8112f9734fab18001bb8394632abf66ca6cfc3ae4ec041e8350850c2c4477b"]}
{"id": "clm:aaab9b6990cf182f8f522001e1d6d7f7a8d6f52809b31dfb9ee945dacdad986b", "type": "statement", "text": "Custom bucketing alone does not establish fixed-bucket optimization eligibility: the query README requires that bucketMaxSpanSeconds and bucketRoundingSeconds have not changed since creation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bc8112f9734fab18001bb8394632abf66ca6cfc3ae4ec041e8350850c2c4477b"]}
{"id": "clm:69d864e8d4647fbad174083f132097ab60e416dd81f6d4352a83425339f89d46", "type": "statement", "text": "An explain COLLSCAN does not imply a scan of individual measurements: Percona demonstrated time equality rewritten into _id and control timestamp bounds on backing buckets in MongoDB 5.0. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/mongodb-5-0-time-series-collections/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6c997b49504d49ebcac59196fd240a675489ea74525e2c37149f37ed69f0b6c9", "ev:8a5ca6725e90434ded9ccb35ee4683e4cb5008d2a7eb7ec50117e12ce0cf0db9"]}
{"id": "clm:db240a95dab86ab4b04a48ec7534e3dde43d24861ded2db1223b641caee4de76", "type": "statement", "text": "A Stack Overflow user independently reported documents available by measurement _id but missing from timestamp ranges, alongside bucket _id/control.min mismatch warnings. The later answer relays MongoDB support; that diagnosis is vendor-origin evidence, not independent corroboration. (low confidence) (verified as of 2024-12-11)", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79141281/mongodb-time-series-collection-fails-to-retrieve-data-when-queried-by-timestamp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1d005bc1be442155826fbf3b627c987a72707e2a4f5557ce656dffd4f095466c", "ev:8ffa95891386ea7d8eb0f1f95f9cdfca34c43a53bb0573591447745ccc0ac7f4"]}
{"id": "clm:d8670a63d2f9570d61ca518f5493906da5ea696762c875e69bd032ff21b7a51b", "type": "statement", "text": "Time-field comparisons can become bucket filters on control.min.<timeField> and control.max.<timeField> before unpacking. Percona independently shows these control comparisons, plus bucket _id bounds, in explain output for timestamp equality and range queries in MongoDB 5.0. Bucket candidates can still require filtering individual measurements. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_spec.h", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/mongodb-5-0-time-series-collections/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6c997b49504d49ebcac59196fd240a675489ea74525e2c37149f37ed69f0b6c9", "ev:7e703f7a7bef14e704aab0224afa92c605e7accb3f31707929ef2e60ee79f3ff", "ev:8a5ca6725e90434ded9ccb35ee4683e4cb5008d2a7eb7ec50117e12ce0cf0db9", "ev:e6243e48f7f3fdeb51f61d8fcbe13fa9a8cd5e77f82397e90b2d63d58e8c3fdd"]}
{"id": "clm:b4e80bfb4f3bd9cddfb5a474c3c40ac7d8acf92fb9d29abe852fd1d1d80cfbd0", "type": "statement", "text": "In the inspected default generator, let t be the Date operand, S=bucketMaxSpanSeconds in duration units, m=control.min.<timeField>, and M=control.max.<timeField>. Equality generates m<=t AND m>=t-S AND M>=t AND M<=t+S. Greater-than generates M>t AND m>t-S; greater-than-or-equal uses >= on both. Less-than generates m<t AND M<t+S; less-than-or-equal uses <= on both. These are bucket candidate tests, not proof that each measurement matches. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5114196c41899fa3f80544f7fc94e7194522df99ca771353be99ef39df45da6b"]}
{"id": "clm:9dc386da7e659891d83f27167b1d88da0985930735c9a90a5234ee3ede7cca98", "type": "statement", "text": "The extra time-span-adjusted comparison is deliberate: for time<t, BucketSpec documents both control.min.time<t and control.max.time<t+bucketMaxSpanSeconds. The implementation explains that span bounds help narrow time-index scans and mongos routing. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_spec.h"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5114196c41899fa3f80544f7fc94e7194522df99ca771353be99ef39df45da6b", "ev:7e703f7a7bef14e704aab0224afa92c605e7accb3f31707929ef2e60ee79f3ff"]}
{"id": "clm:c9b57e623458b4d78bb0369389360e5a8bffa1d4145a8808845fe24a4a42970c", "type": "statement", "text": "The inspected comparison generator requires a Date operand for the actual timeField and declines comparisons against non-Date values. It also rejects mapping fields computed by an earlier $addFields/computed projection or removed by projection. Treat a displayed time-like field as eligible only after checking its actual bucket specification and pipeline provenance. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aa5c818875a3d5754badf878ff403be3a3dec0082d0444bdecc4d77355f35967"]}
{"id": "clm:d2b1149f824e1c92afec0a3dac6f991cb2eb64f6482419efc556cb8120c73e54", "type": "statement", "text": "With unchanged fixed bucketing, the generator can replace the default t-S lower bound on control.min.time with t rounded down to the fixed interval. Boundary-aligned $gte and $lt predicates can provide an exact bucket selection and permit removal of event filtering; $gt, $lte, and equality retain event filtering. The inspected builder disables fixed-bucket specialization for extended-range data. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_level_comparison_predicate_generator.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/bucket_spec.h", "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/query/timeseries/README.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0b2824b18859b0f8a6d239ffae7c224c261395385b60d5b1d4180eaa5fa29462", "ev:75dc5e55893de9154f98bfeabdd2f75e28d7ac406683c33fabf311c89bb4fc04", "ev:bc8112f9734fab18001bb8394632abf66ca6cfc3ae4ec041e8350850c2c4477b"]}
{"id": "clm:f8690a1e1d3b26b9b0331a8aa47ad1914b245145fe6fc3eb4a3b935142abe318", "type": "statement", "text": "A Stack Overflow user independently reports that a time-range query omitted documents retrievable by measurement _id, and that export/reimport restored results. This is a firsthand symptom report, not independent proof of the optimizer formulas; the same page later quotes MongoDB support for its deletion-related diagnosis. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79141281/mongodb-time-series-collection-fails-to-retrieve-data-when-queried-by-timestamp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Time-field bucket predicates"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:040691e653b9c3b0472e1e89595dbe18cf183c6e8c286d09f55f2655fe69f402", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1d005bc1be442155826fbf3b627c987a72707e2a4f5557ce656dffd4f095466c", "ev:8ffa95891386ea7d8eb0f1f95f9cdfca34c43a53bb0573591447745ccc0ac7f4"]}
